  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B012",
        "laureates": [
          "Ian H. Frazer",
          "John T. Schiller",
          "Douglas R. Lowy"
        ],
        "citation": "for virus-like-particle vaccines that prevent HPV infection and related cancers"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B014",
    "B006"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B012 most convincingly combines a bounded biological and technological principle with exceptionally mature prevention of HPV infection and related cancers. Its consequence is direct, durable, and established clinically and in public health. Frazer, Schiller, and Lowy remain a plausible three-person allocation when the achievement is confined to foundational virus-like-particle vaccine work rather than the entire subsequent development and delivery enterprise.",
    "case_against": "The proposed trio cannot represent all indispensable contributions to papillomavirus biology, clinical development, manufacturing, implementation, and population-level delivery. The citation must therefore be read narrowly as recognizing the VLP vaccine principle. B014 remains a very close alternative because it links important physiology to broad, established therapeutic benefit.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann argues that B014's GLP-1 physiology provides a coherent discovery-to-therapy chain with exceptionally consequential and mature benefits in diabetes and obesity, while recognizing difficult credit boundaries involving later drug development.",
        "response": "I agree that the physiological insight and medical impact make B014 a leading alternative. The chair's question sharpens the remaining problem: a citation that claims to have enabled transformative therapies must distinguish foundational GLP-1 work from consequential medicinal-chemistry and industrial contributions, including the further credited candidate. A narrowly framed physiology citation may be defensible, but it would capture less of the stated therapeutic achievement. B012 permits a more direct alignment among citation, proposed names, and mature medical outcome."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius favors B042 as a fundamental, broadly explanatory discovery of cGAS-STING-mediated cytosolic DNA sensing, while acknowledging unresolved allocation among five credited scientists and uneven clinical translation.",
        "response": "I share the view that B042 is a major fundamental discovery with wide biological reach. However, the supplied discussion does not resolve the relative claims of Chen, Barber, Ishikawa, Wu, and Sun under the three-person limit. In comparison, B012 has both a more settled proposed allocation and a direct, established preventive consequence. I therefore continue to give greater weight to mature medical benefit where the fundamental-discovery case is also clear."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record can delimit the B012 laureates' foundational VLP contributions sufficiently precisely from later vaccine development, trials, manufacturing, and implementation.",
      "Whether B014 can be framed around GLP-1 physiology and its enabling role without understating indispensable later therapeutic-development contributions.",
      "Whether the five-person attribution issue for B042 can be resolved more securely than the supplied discussion permits."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent with the proposed laureates or shortlisted achievements from the supplied profile. My documented coauthorship in spatial transcriptomics and other research collaborations does not identify a connection to the proposed configuration."
  }
}
